NAME
       tr - translate or delete characters

SYNOPSIS
       tr [-dsc] SET1 [SET2]

DESCRIPTION
       Translate, squeeze and/or delete characters from standard input. SETs
       may contain ranges (a-z), escapes (\n \t) and classes ([:upper:]
       [:digit:] [:space:] ...).

OPTIONS
       -d
           delete characters in SET1

       -s
           squeeze repeated characters into one

       -c
           use the complement of SET1

EXAMPLES
       echo hello | tr a-z A-Z
       tr -d '\r' < dos.txt > unix.txt
       tr -s ' '

SEE ALSO
       cut(1)
